%description:

Tcp.keepAliveIdleTime:rfc -- the first probe comes 7200 s after the last segment.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "the idle time before the first keepalive probe (RFC 9293 MUST-28: at
least two hours; Linux tcp_keepalive_time)".

The classes: rfc (7200 s, the default: the two hours of RFC 9293 MUST-28) and other (another
value). The code: TcpAlgorithmBase::processKeepAliveTimer() sends the first probe when the
connection has received no segment for the value. This test separates "rfc" from the other value.

Host under test: host1, with keepalive (precondition); host1 sends 10000 bytes at 0.2 s and then nothing; host2 sends nothing. A keepalive probe is a
segment without data with SEG.SEQ = SND.UNA - 1. Observation: level 1, the first probe
comes 7200 s after the ACK of the data, and not before.

%# parameter: Tcp.keepAliveIdleTime
%# class: rfc
%# value: 7200s
%# key: *.host1.tcp.keepAliveIdleTime
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpKeepAliveIdleTimeRfc")
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.ackNo == {isn} + 1 + 10000")
             .describe("the ACK of all data of host1: the idle time starts")
             .within(1.0))
        .never(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
              .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 10000 && pk.dataLength <= tcp.headerLength")
              .describe("an early keepalive probe")
              .within(7199.9))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 10000 && pk.dataLength <= tcp.headerLength")
             .describe("keepalive probe")
             .within(0.2));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpKeepAliveIdleTimeRfc compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.keepAliveIdleTime = 7200s    # the parameter under test
*.host1.tcp.keepAliveEnabled = true
*.host1.app[0].tClose = 10000s
sim-time-limit = 7202s
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpKeepAliveIdleTimeRfc: PASS
